# W0.6 — kept out of every image's build context. "Getting node_modules out is not optional" (brief
# Recon): a host node_modules can carry a Windows-built better-sqlite3/.node or the wrong
# @resvg/resvg-js optional dependency, and COPYing it into a Linux image is the classic way to ship
# a binary the container can't load. Every install in the Dockerfiles runs `pnpm install` fresh,
# inside the image, against the platform it's actually building for.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# VCS / editor / OS noise.
.git
.gitignore
.vs
.idea

# Build outputs and caches — regenerated inside the image by each Dockerfile's own `pnpm build`.
# Leaving a host-built copy in the context risks a stale/host-platform artifact silently riding
# along a COPY of its parent directory instead of the fresh one the container build produces.
dist
**/dist
build
apps/web/build
.svelte-kit
**/.svelte-kit
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage

# Local runtime state and secrets — never belongs in an image.
artifacts
*.db
*.db-*
.env
.env.*
data
**/data

# Sibling worktrees the brief calls out explicitly (not reachable from this build context anyway,
# since Docker can't COPY outside it, but excluded defensively in case the context root ever moves).
pc-parts-inventory-wt

# Not needed inside either image.
docs
.claude
